Questions & Answers
Give one point of difference between individual supply and market supply.
Individual supply may not strictly follow Law of supply, i.e. it is not necessary that
supply for an individual always varies directly with price. However, market supply
always follows law of supply, i.e. market supply always varies directly with price.
