Questions & Answers
Explain any two factors that cause a(shift of supply curve.
Two factors that cause a shift of supply curve are
Change in Technology Technological improvement tends to lower the marginal and
average costs of production because better technology facilitates higher output with the
same inputs. Accordingly, producers are willing to supply more at the existing price. This
implies a rightward shift in supply curve and vice-versa.
(ii) Change in Input Price When the price of inputs increases, the costs of production also
increase, leading producers to supply less at the current price, causing a leftward shift in
the supply curve. Conversely, a decrease in input prices lowers production costs and results
in producers supplying more at the existing price, shifting the supply curve to the right.
